  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1038 PM CST TUE NOV 17 2026\n\nWednesday through Saturday\n\nAn upper-level low positioned near the northeastern Gulf Coast\nwill maintain cloud cover across southern and eastern portions of\nthe area through late week. Given dry low-level profiles,\nmeasurable precipitation is unlikely, though isolated sprinkles\nor light showers remain possible. High temperatures will linger\nslightly below seasonal normals under cloud cover, with mild\novernight lows south. The low weakens and drifts northeast Friday\ninto Saturday morning, allowing rain chances to diminish and\ntemperatures to moderate over the weekend.\n\nSunday through Monday\n\nA cold front is forecast to traverse the region on Sunday. Model\nguidance continues to trend drier with this frontal passage,\nsuggesting primary impacts will be limited to a wind shift. In\nthe wake of the front, zonal flow aloft and surface high pressure\nbuilding into the region will maintain dry conditions into early\nnext week.\n\n16",
